<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Maritime Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Serdang Sultanate</h1><p class="st-meta">1723 CE – 1946 CE (approx.) · capital Perbaungan</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Malay sultanate of eastern Sumatra that split from Deli in 1723 and shared in the plantation wealth of the colonial era.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Serdang arose from a succession dispute in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/deli-sultanate">Deli Sultanate</a> after the death of Tuanku Panglima Paderap around 1723. One of his sons, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuanku-umar-johan-alamsyah">Tuanku Umar Johan Alamsyah</a>, was passed over and withdrew with local support to found a separate realm on the Serdang river, south-east of Deli.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sultans ruled Malay coastal communities and drew tribute from neighbouring <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karo-batak">Karo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simalungun-people">Simalungun Batak</a> lands. Like Deli, Serdang came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> control in the 1860s and leased land for tobacco and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a> estates. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Sulaiman Shariful Alamshah, who reigned from 1881 to 1946, was known as a patron of Malay arts and education.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Serdang survived as a self-governing domain of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/dutch-east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-sumatra-revolution">East Sumatran social revolution</a> of March 1946, when the Malay aristocracy lost its power and the sultanate was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/indonesia">Republic of Indonesia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/serdang-sultanate.jpg" alt="Serdang Sultanate" width="320" height="189"><figcaption>Image: Kesultanan dan Kerajaan Di Indonesia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultanate_of_Serdang_Flag.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1723 CE – 1946 CE (approx.